<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Les Andelys</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Les Andelys is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eure">Eure</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Normandy. Above it stands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chateau-gaillard">Château Gaillard</a>, built by Richard the Lionheart in 1196–1198 to defend Normandy against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-france">Philip II of France</a> and taken by the French in 1204 after a long siege. The painter Nicolas Poussin was born nearby in 1594.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/les-andelys.jpg" alt="Les Andelys" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Casper Moller · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LesAndelys.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
